{"title":"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c81ffa59a374578a1dba99ad772902ea17ebadb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+2^{x}+2^{2x+1}= y^{2}.\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution then obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed846ce2d35162698b1eab724ba240718789fd93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6b9bd52c88cbb204949d2862b6673ae286512e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is a solution too.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> we get the two solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0ef68f274ec95f4a8f94eebff49accdcf689ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb3399f288c7a28ac2484b7bba72654ee4d9772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> be a solution with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />; without loss of generality confine attention to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6267cf18ccdbddb223019a94263e5b80bafe617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />.  The equation rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9e8901ad5441dbe1e0aff4dc4378de6c26d386.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^x(1+2^{x+1}) = (y-1)(y+1)\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"19\" /> shows that the factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851018537a4268dffd3e893158af5b7d9f3aeb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f801b9f0ef3c2c1d614cd42c8abd34ebedf7c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> are even, exactly one of them divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54dcc403405dfb565d57d1d25afa13cd6bffc603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and one  of these factors is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345963566df529efe09d653a6a740743a345d9f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{x-1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065d0462782004d830c2bfbda340ff333d710f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />.  So\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74169ecdf7dbb7f69067cfba17f2c469e80cf381.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = 2^{x-1}m + \\varepsilon, \\qquad m\\text{ odd},\\qquad \\varepsilon = \\pm 1.\\qquad\\qquad(*)\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"19\" />\nPlugging this into the original equation we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1123199dff56c5a920c67784125ce6deccdae9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^x(1+2^{x+1}) = (2^{x+1}m + \\varepsilon)^2 - 1 = 2^{2x-2}m^2 + 2^xm\\varepsilon,\\]\" width=\"411\" height=\"19\" />\nor, equivalently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c87e529bd3c4b393297fb358b6ffb4d5da658ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 2^{x+1} = 2^{x-2}m^2 + m\\varepsilon.\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a0889c4452b4acf0137d9a5b12be40112549300f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 - \\varepsilon m = 2^{x-2}(m^2 - 8).\\qquad(\\dagger)\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" /> For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e058cdd81905f61b5726ff5fb7be1c2171ff9aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> this yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e7bb40b0fc35ecdfe316c01a450a7204702999c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - 8 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b5800f5ad040d308609190ef18a9e0ca08a9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, which fails to satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7ba85cf5f0d70b74a834774f52d0b7ab9ec32dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\dagger)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43369716b4d8f776adfec896b88c503aa920204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7ba85cf5f0d70b74a834774f52d0b7ab9ec32dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\dagger)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21c42e694525621d7b353aa328d94fb540332650.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + m = 2^{x-2}(m^2 - 8) \\geq 2(m^2 - 8),\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"19\" /> implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f1b76321f1cf592488174b8c5df714813c5aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m^2 - m - 17 \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />.  Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd65f1b40c2880eca6023f65483d90ddd49cc36a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\leq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />; on the other hand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7ba85cf5f0d70b74a834774f52d0b7ab9ec32dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\dagger)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435f596415f58ca7262e69549ba5300a10fa2736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />.  These values indeed satisfy the given equation.  Recall that then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/8666e66b4800e41869814d052b55a5df1995265f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> is also good.  Thus we have the complete list of solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0ef68f274ec95f4a8f94eebff49accdcf689ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb3399f288c7a28ac2484b7bba72654ee4d9772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5606b857e20929512f1495d21a0e6ac8611b5068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c3457eb701ad0a3efb5cc6a487160a607a0d9c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,-23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO\" title=\"2006 IMO\">2006 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211729\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 260/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8021/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.914      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.914      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11408:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211729 and revision id 204525. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}